// Edge layer for worthmydegree.com — deployed as Cloudflare Worker
// "wmd-edge" on routes worthmydegree.com/* and www.worthmydegree.com/*.
//
// Jobs, in order:
//   1. Canonicalize host + scheme (www and http 301 to the https apex).
//   2. Serve /robots.txt, /sitemap.xml, /llms.txt (Streamlit cannot serve
//      root-path files, so the edge does).
//   3. Pass Streamlit internals (/_stcore websocket + health, static
//      assets) through UNTOUCHED — breaking these hangs the app.
//   4. 301 stray paths to / (the app has exactly one route).
//   5. Inject <link rel=canonical>, meta description, and Organization/
//      WebApplication JSON-LD into the HTML shell; add a Link: canonical
//      response header. Tracking params (src/test/admin/research/from)
//      are stripped from the CANONICAL VALUE ONLY — the request itself is
//      never rewritten, so share links and attribution are unaffected.
//
// The served text files live beside this file, and they are no longer all the
// same kind of thing:
//
//   infra/llms.txt    SOURCE. Edit it; `python3 infra/build_site.py` copies it
//                     into the LLMS constant and regenerates its guide list.
//   infra/sitemap.xml SOURCE for everything outside its generated guide block,
//                     which the same build regenerates in both halves.
//   infra/robots.txt  Reference copy only. Still hand-kept in step with the
//                     ROBOTS constant below, so change both in the same PR.
//
// The two generated ones were hand-kept too, and the instruction to do it
// lived only in this comment. Nothing checked, and a stale half is invisible:
// the file still serves, still parses, and simply describes an older site.
//
// Do NOT spell either injection marker out in a comment here, in any file the
// build injects into. An earlier version of this block quoted the sitemap's
// opening marker while explaining what it was for. That put the marker's FIRST
// occurrence above the SITEMAP constant, so the next build replaced everything
// from this comment down to the real closing marker with sitemap XML and
// worker.js stopped being JavaScript. Every check in the repo still passed:
// they read the generated pages, and the pages were fine. build_site.py now
// runs `node --check` on its own output before writing, which is what caught
// it -- twice, because the first attempt at this very warning quoted the
// marker again.

